2.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujan2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.openssl.org/news/secadv/20190910.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/154467/Slackware-Security-Advisory-openssl-Updates.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190919-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.tenable.com/security/tns-2019-09","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://git.openssl.org/gitweb/?p=openssl.git%3Ba=commitdiff%3Bh=08229ad838c50f644d7e928e2eef147b4308ad64","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://git.openssl.org/gitweb/?p=openssl.git%3Ba=commitdiff%3Bh=631f94db0065c78181ca9ba5546ebc8bb3884b97","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://git.openssl.org/gitweb/?p=openssl.git%3Ba=commitdiff%3Bh=e21f8cf78a125cd3c8c0d1a1a6c8bb0b901f893f","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://support.f5.com/csp/article/K97324400?utm_source=f5support&amp%3Butm_medium=RSS","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4376-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4376-2"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4504-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4504-1"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuoct2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://kc.mcafee.com/corporate/index?page=content&id=SB10365","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"credits":["Bernd Edlinger"],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-5592","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"fortinet","published":"2019-08-23T19:52:17.000Z","updated":"2024-10-25T14:05:55.461Z","description":"Multiple padding oracle vulnerabilities (Zombie POODLE, GOLDENDOODLE, OpenSSL 0-length) in the CBC padding implementation of FortiOS IPS engine version 5.000 to 5.006, 4.000 to 4.036, 4.200 to 4.219, 3.547 and below, when configured with SSL Deep Inspection policies and with the IPS sensor enabled, may allow an attacker to decipher TLS connections going through the FortiGate via monitoring the traffic in a Man-in-the-middle position.","cwe":["Information disclosure"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"Fortinet IPS Engine","versions":["affected IPS engine version 5.000 to 5.006, 4.000 to 4.036, 4.200 to 4.219, 3.547 and below"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://fortiguard.com/advisory/FG-IR-19-145","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["fortinet","openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-12572","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-06-21T17:51:16.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T23:24:39.151Z","description":"A vulnerability in the London Trust Media Private Internet Access (PIA) VPN Client 1.0.2 (build 02363) for Windows could allow an authenticated, local attacker to run arbitrary code with elevated privileges. On startup, the PIA Windows service (pia-service.exe) loads the OpenSSL library from %PROGRAMFILES%\\Private Internet Access\\libeay32.dll. This library attempts to load the C:\\etc\\ssl\\openssl.cnf configuration file which does not exist. By default on Windows systems, authenticated users can create directories under C:\\. A low privileged user can create a C:\\etc\\ssl\\openssl.cnf configuration file to load a malicious OpenSSL engine library resulting in arbitrary code execution as SYSTEM when the service starts.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/mirchr/security-research/blob/master/vulnerabilities/PIA/CVE-2019-12572.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://blog.mirch.io/2019/06/10/cve-2019-12572-pia-windows-privilege-escalation-malicious-openssl-engine/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["microsoft","openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-17185","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-03-21T00:13:05.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T01:33:17.262Z","description":"In FreeRADIUS 3.0.x before 3.0.20, the EAP-pwd module used a global OpenSSL BN_CTX instance to handle all handshakes. This mean multiple threads use the same BN_CTX instance concurrently, resulting in crashes when concurrent EAP-pwd handshakes are initiated. This can be abused by an adversary as a Denial-of-Service (DoS) attack.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://freeradius.org/security/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/releases/tag/release_3_0_20","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2020-04/msg00039.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2020:0553"}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-19269","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-11-26T03:34:24.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T02:09:39.567Z","description":"An issue was discovered in tls_verify_crl in ProFTPD through 1.3.6b. A dereference of a NULL pointer may occur. This pointer is returned by the OpenSSL sk_X509_REVOKED_value() function when encountering an empty CRL installed by a system administrator. The dereference occurs when validating the certificate of a client connecting to the server in a TLS client/server mutual-authentication setup.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/proftpd/proftpd/issues/861","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2019/11/msg00039.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20191130 [SECURITY] [DLA 2018-1] proftpd-dfsg security update"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/OGBBCPLJSDPFG5EI5P5G7P4KEX7YSD5G/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2019-65a983b8b6"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/QR65XUHPCRU3NXTSFVF2J4GWRIHC7AHW/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2019-bfacf1e958"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2020-01/msg00009.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2020:0031"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202003-35","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202003-35"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuapr2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
